   "evidence": "Proof body at Elastic/FormFactor/Basic.lean:184-187 is `by_contra hu; exact hS.anisotropic u hpu hp'u hu (hJ.apply_spectator_self_eq_zero hSymm hpu hp'u)` \u2014 `hS.span`/`hS.toIsSpectatorSplit` never appears.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/Elastic/FormFactor/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Replace `hS : SpectatorAssumptions g p p'` with `(hani : \u2200 u : V, g p u = 0 \u2192 g p' u = 0 \u2192 u \u2260 0 \u2192 g u u \u2260 0)` and call `hani u hpu hp'u hu` in the proof; `exists_eq_smul_add_smul` then passes `hS.anisotropic`. If the predicate is wanted as a named object, put it next to `Bilin.IsSpectatorSplit` \u2014 DIS already restates the same predicate in `SpectatorAssumptions.self_ne_zero_of_spectator` (DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean:977).",
   "issue": "`IsLorentzCovariant.spectator_eq_zero` takes `hS : SpectatorAssumptions g p p'` but its proof projects only `hS.anisotropic`; the `Bilin.IsSpectatorSplit` field is unused, so the lemma is unusable where anisotropy is known but no splitting is. The two lemmas in this repo that perform the same reflection-kills-the-spectator step both take the anisotropy bare: `covariant_spectator_offDiagonal_zero` (DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean:702, `hu : u \u2260 0 \u2192 g u u \u2260 0`) and `ParityOdd.eq_zero_of_isLorentzCovariant` (ParityOdd.lean:263, `hnull : \u2200 u, ... \u2192 g u u \u2260 0` alongside a separate `hS : Bilin.IsSpectatorSplit`), the latter edited by this PR.",
   "line": 182
  }
 ],
